From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 10:29:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/22] libcameraservice: buffer-queue video mode for the HAL1
 CameraClient

Android's CameraSource now records only in VIDEO_BUFFER_MODE_BUFFER_QUEUE:
it hands the camera a video target (its own BufferQueue) and waits for frames
there. The restored HAL1 CameraClient refused both setVideoTarget() and that
mode, so CameraSource came up without a format and droidmedia's recorder
crashed on it.

Accept the mode and the target. The HAL keeps delivering its YUV recording
frames (NV21) through the data callback; each one is copied into a buffer of
the target, in the plane layout gralloc gave it, queued with the frame's
timestamp and released to the HAL at once. The target is asked for
IMPLEMENTATION_DEFINED buffers with rare CPU writes, so gralloc picks the
encoder's layout and maps them uncached: the encoder reads them by DMA, and an
unlock that leaves the CPU cache dirty gave green frames.

A HAL without metadata support rejects storeMetaDataInBuffers(false) too (the
HP TouchPad's answers BAD_VALUE); turning metadata off is what YUV frames need,
so that is not treated as an error.

Tested on the HP TouchPad (msm8660 HAL1): hardware H.264 recordings at 640x480
with a correct picture.

Change-Id: I40b9da4cf387981aa5a08dbe8a7b76e2f05cd016
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
